# Order Management API - VS Code REST Client
# Run the authentication requests first, then numbered requests. Credentials are prompted, not committed.
# CUSTOMER creates/reads its own orders. ADMIN performs catalog/inventory/lifecycle actions.
# Named responses supply real IDs, including when the database already has data.
# Create requests add records each time they are sent. Change baseUrl if needed.
# Guided presentation: auth -> 01-13 -> 19/21 -> 33 + the named fulfillment retry -> 35 -> 38 -> 39 -> 42.
# Then 68/69 for order listing, 46/47 for history, 80-89 for deactivation, 96/97/98 for signed adjustments,
# and 90/91 to reactivate. Request 33 starts at stock 20 when run after cancellation 11; other paths may have different stock.
# scripts/demo.ps1 is the fully automated, isolated-per-run version with assertions and actual returned IDs.
# Documentation: https://github.com/Huachao/vscode-restclient#request-variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@customerToken = {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@keyboardId = {{createKeyboard.response.body.$.id}}
@mouseId = {{createMouse.response.body.$.id}}
@orderId = {{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}
@unusedProductId = {{createUnusedProduct.response.body.$.id}}
@fulfillmentOrderId = {{createFulfillmentOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Authentication: Register CUSTOMER once (409 if email already exists)
# @name registerCustomer
# @prompt customerEmail Enter your local CUSTOMER email
# @prompt password Enter your local CUSTOMER password (12-72 characters, at most 72 UTF-8 bytes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{customerEmail}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Authentication: Login CUSTOMER; repeat after token expiry
# @name loginCustomer
# @prompt customerEmail Enter your registered local CUSTOMER email
# @prompt password Enter your local CUSTOMER password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{customerEmail}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Authentication: Login ADMIN provisioned by explicit operator bootstrap
# @name loginAdmin
# @prompt adminEmail Enter your local ADMIN email
# @prompt password Enter your local ADMIN password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{adminEmail}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### 01. Create Product: keyboard -> 201 + Location; stock 20
# @name createKeyboard
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "USB keyboard",
  "price": 59.90,
  "stockQuantity": 20
}

### 02. Create Product: mouse -> 201 + Location; stock 10
# @name createMouse
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mouse",
  "description": "USB mouse",
  "price": 19.99,
  "stockQuantity": 10
}

### 03. List Products -> 200; zero-based pagination, ascending ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=0&size=10

### 04. Get Product -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 05. Update Product -> 200; PUT accepts metadata only, without stockQuantity
# Run before creating the order. Prices remain consistent with the README example.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "USB keyboard",
  "price": 59.90
}

### 06. Create Order -> 201 + Location; total 139.79; remaining stock 18 / 9
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": {{mouseId}}, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 07. Get Order -> 200; status CREATED, total 139.79
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 08. Validation Error -> 400; fieldErrors contains items[0].quantity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 0 }
  ]
}

### 09. Insufficient Stock Error -> 409; requested 21, available 18
# Run before cancellation. No order is created and no stock is deducted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 21 }
  ]
}

### 10. Duplicate Product Error -> 400; duplicate productId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 11. Cancel Order -> 200; status CANCELLED; restored stock 20 / 10
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12. Cancel Again -> 409; stock must not be restored twice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13. Confirm Restored Stock -> 200; stockQuantity 20
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 14. Delete Referenced Product -> 409, even after cancellation
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15. Create a product with zero stock -> 201; INITIAL_STOCK history is still recorded
# @name createUnusedProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Disposable sample product",
  "description": "Used only by this request sequence",
  "price": 1.00,
  "stockQuantity": 0
}

### 16. Delete Product With Inventory History -> 409, even when initial stock is zero
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{unusedProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 17. Get Retained Product -> 200; deletion was refused to preserve history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{unusedProductId}}

### 18. Invalid Pagination -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=-1&size=101

### 19. Search Product Name -> 200; case-insensitive substring
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?keyword=KEYboard

### 20. Filter Inclusive Price Range -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=19.99&maxPrice=59.90&sort=price,asc

### 21. Combine Every Filter -> 200; only matching in-stock keyboards
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?keyword=keyboard&minPrice=20&maxPrice=100&inStock=true&page=0&size=10&sort=price,asc

### 22. Available Products -> 200; stockQuantity > 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?inStock=true&sort=stockQuantity,desc

### 23. Unavailable Products -> 200; stockQuantity = 0; may be empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?inStock=false

### 24. Upper Price Bound Only and Name Sorting -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?maxPrice=30&sort=name,desc

### 25. Second Filtered Page -> 200; totalElements counts all matching products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=0&page=1&size=1&sort=price,asc

### 26. Literal Percent Search -> 200; matches names containing 50%, may be empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?keyword=50%25

### 27. Negative Price Bound -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=-0.01

### 28. Reversed Price Range -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=100&maxPrice=20

### 29. Unsupported Sort Field -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?sort=description,asc

### 30. Unsupported Sort Direction -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?sort=price,up

### 31. Page Size Above Limit -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?size=101

### 32. Invalid Parameter Type -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=abc

### 33. Create a separate order for fulfillment -> 201; keyboard stock 20 -> 19
# @name createFulfillmentOrder
# The order from request 06 was cancelled; do not reuse it for this sequence.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: portfolio-fulfillment-{{keyboardId}}

{
  "items": [{ "productId": {{keyboardId}}, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Retry the fulfillment creation before advancing its lifecycle -> 200, same ID, no extra stock deduction
# @name retryFulfillmentOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: portfolio-fulfillment-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1}]}

### 34. Ship Before Confirmation -> 409; remains CREATED, stock 19
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 35. Confirm -> 200; CREATED -> CONFIRMED, stock stays 19
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 36. Confirm Again -> 409; no repeated transition
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 37. Cancel Confirmed Order -> 409; stock must not be restored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 38. Ship -> 200; CONFIRMED -> SHIPPED, stock stays 19
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 39. Deliver -> 200; SHIPPED -> DELIVERED, stock stays 19
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 40. Deliver Again -> 409; DELIVERED is terminal
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 41. Cancel Delivered Order -> 409; stock must not be restored
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 42. Get Delivered Order -> 200; original price, total, items, and createdAt retained
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{fulfillmentOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 43. Verify Stock After Fulfillment -> 200; stockQuantity stays 19
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 44. Confirm Previously Cancelled Order -> 409; cancelled order cannot be revived
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 45. Manual Restock -> 200; keyboard stock 19 -> 24, journal records +5 and reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/restock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":5,"reason":"Supplier delivery"}

### 46. Latest Inventory Movements -> 200; newest first, with product/order IDs and stock snapshots
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/stock-movements?page=0&size=10&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 47. Inventory History Oldest First -> 200; INITIAL, -2, +2, -1, +5 in this sequence
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/stock-movements?page=0&size=10&sort=createdAt,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 48. Invalid Restock Quantity -> 400; no inventory movement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/restock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":0,"reason":"Invalid quantity example"}

### 49. Missing Restock Reason -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/restock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":1}

### 50. Invalid Inventory History Sorting -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/stock-movements?sort=quantityDelta,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 51. Product PUT Rejects Unknown Stock Field -> 400; stock and history remain unchanged
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Mechanical Keyboard","description":"USB keyboard","price":59.90,"stockQuantity":0}


### 52. Create Order With Idempotency-Key -> 201; keyboard stock 24 -> 23
# @name createIdempotentOrder
# Change this key for a NEW intended order; retain it for retries 53-56.
# It uses the keyboard ID so rerunning the initial product fixtures uses a different key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keyboard-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1}]}

### 53. Retry Same Key and Payload -> 200; same order ID/body, stock stays 23
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keyboard-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"quantity":1,"productId":{{keyboardId}}}]}

### 54. Same Key With Different Quantity -> 409; no extra order or deduction
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keyboard-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":2}]}

### 55. Cancel the Keyed Order -> 200; keyboard stock 23 -> 24
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createIdempotentOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 56. Retry Creation After Cancellation -> 200; original CREATED snapshot, no stock change
# GET the order URL to see its current CANCELLED state.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keyboard-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1}]}

### 57. Invalid Idempotency-Key -> 400; no key reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: invalid key with spaces

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1}]}

### 58. Failed Creation Does Not Consume Key -> 409 insufficient stock
# The failed key can be retried after sufficient restock, or used with corrected input.
# A committed successful key would instead reject changed input.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-retry-after-error-{{keyboardId}}

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1000000}]}


### 59. Swagger UI -> 200 HTML
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui/index.html

### 60. OpenAPI 3 specification -> 200 JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs

### 61. Health -> 200 with status only when healthy
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### 62. Missing Bearer Token -> 401; no order lookup or stock write
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 63. CUSTOMER Cannot Restock -> 403; no stock/journal write
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/restock
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":1,"reason":"Forbidden customer operation"}

### 64. CUSTOMER Cannot Cancel Even Its Own Order -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 65. Login Another CUSTOMER -> 200; register that account separately first
# @name loginOtherCustomer
# @prompt otherEmail Enter a different registered CUSTOMER email
# @prompt password Enter that local CUSTOMER password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{otherEmail}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### 66. Another Customer Cannot Read the First Customer's Order -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOtherCustomer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 67. Registration Cannot Select ADMIN -> 400
# @prompt newEmail Enter an unused local email
# @prompt password Enter a local test password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{newEmail}}","password":"{{password}}","role":"ADMIN"}

### 68. List Own Orders -> 200; summaries only, newest createdAt then ID first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 69. ADMIN List All Orders -> 200; includes legacy orders without an owner
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 70. Filter Own Orders by Status and Inclusive Time Range -> 200
# Adjust the dates to match your local demo records. No userId query parameter is needed or accepted as an owner filter.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?status=CREATED&from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-30T23:59:59Z&page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 71. Second Page of Own Orders -> 200; totalElements still counts all matching own orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?page=1&size=1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 72. No Orders in an Old Time Range -> 200 with empty content
# Assumes your database has no orders from this illustrative historical period.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?from=2000-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2000-01-02T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 73. List Orders Without a Bearer Token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

### 74. Invalid Order Status -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?status=UNKNOWN
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 75. Reversed Time Range -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?from=2026-11-30T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 76. Oversized Page -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?size=101
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 77. JPA Offset Overflow -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?page=2147483647&size=100
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 78. Numeric Timezone Offset -> 200; same instant as 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?from=2026-11-01T07:00:00%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 79. Another CUSTOMER Lists Only Its Own Orders -> 200, never the first customer's orders
# Run loginOtherCustomer first. Empty content is valid when this second account has no orders.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOtherCustomer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 80. ADMIN Deactivate Product -> 200; stock and movements unchanged
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"active":false}

### 81. Repeat Deactivation -> 200; no duplicate stock or history write
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"active":false}

### 82. Public Product Detail Is Hidden -> 404, even for ADMIN on this public route
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 83. Public Search Cannot Select Inactive Products -> 200, active records only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?active=false&keyword=keyboard

### 84. ADMIN Find Inactive Products -> 200 with active=false in each result
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products?active=false&keyword=keyboard&page=0&size=20&sort=id,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 85. ADMIN Catalog Without Active Filter -> 200, active and inactive products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 86. Inactive Product Cannot Be Purchased -> 409; no stock/order/receipt write
# After request 90 reactivates it, retry this same key/body to create the order.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: availability-retry-{{keyboardId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"items":[{"productId":{{keyboardId}},"quantity":1}]}

### 87. Existing Order Remains Readable After Product Deactivation -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 88. CUSTOMER Cannot Change Availability -> 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"active":true}

### 89. CUSTOMER Cannot Read ADMIN Catalog -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products?active=false
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 90. ADMIN Reactivate Product -> 200; stock unchanged
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"active":true}

### 91. Reactivated Product Is Public Again -> 200, active=true
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 92. Missing Active Value -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 93. Anonymous ADMIN Catalog Request -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products?active=false

### 94. Metadata PUT After Inventory Changes -> 200; no current stock value is needed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Mechanical Keyboard","description":"Metadata edit after inventory changes","price":59.90}

### Read current stock for the following legacy PUT example
# @name getCurrentProductStock
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}

### 95. PUT Rejects Stock Even If It Equals the Current Value -> 400
# Run getCurrentProductStock first. The old PUT contract is intentionally rejected.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Mechanical Keyboard","description":"Legacy payload","price":59.90,"stockQuantity":{{getCurrentProductStock.response.body.$.stockQuantity}}}

### 96. ADMIN Increase Stock by Adjustment -> 200, MANUAL_ADJUSTMENT history entry
# Not idempotent: every successful execution applies the delta again, even with Idempotency-Key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":5,"reason":"Stock count correction"}

### 97. ADMIN Decrease Stock by Adjustment -> 200 if at least 3 remain; otherwise 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":-3,"reason":"Damaged products"}

### 98. Inspect Adjustment History -> 200, signed delta, before/after, reason and no reference order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/stock-movements?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 99. Reject Zero Adjustment -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":0,"reason":"No change"}

### 100. Reject Blank Adjustment Reason -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":-1,"reason":" "}

### 101. Reject Negative Result -> 409; stock and history unchanged
# Even maximum INTEGER stock cannot accommodate this negative delta.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":-2147483648,"reason":"Would make stock negative"}

### 102. Reject Stock Overflow -> 409 when current stock is positive
# For stock=0 this valid delta reaches Integer.MAX_VALUE and succeeds. Check current stock first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":2147483647,"reason":"Would exceed storage capacity when stock is positive"}

### 103. CUSTOMER Cannot Adjust Stock -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":-1,"reason":"Damaged products"}

### 104. Anonymous Cannot Adjust Stock -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{keyboardId}}/adjust-stock
Content-Type: application/json

{"delta":1,"reason":"Stock count correction"}
